WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:02.658
Possessives and plurals.

00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:04.803
Apostrophes show ownership.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:05.994
They never make plurals.

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:09.459
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.459 --> 00:00:13.829
The choices are the same word, with the apostrophe moved around.

00:00:13.829 --> 00:00:16.677
And the word is usually followed by something it might own.

00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:20.689
It's testing whether you can tell a plural from a possessive.

00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:23.228
Here's the method.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:26.253
Ask: does this word own the next word?

00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:28.663
If not, no apostrophe.

00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:31.213
Is there one owner, or many?

00:00:31.213 --> 00:00:32.783
Look for clues.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.323
One owner gets apostrophe s.

00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:37.783
Many owners get s apostrophe.

00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:41.686
And pronouns like its, their, and whose never take an apostrophe.

00:00:42.798 --> 00:00:46.018
Rule one: a plain plural is just s.

00:00:46.018 --> 00:00:49.128
If nothing is owned, there's no apostrophe.

00:00:49.128 --> 00:00:50.058
The plants bloom.

00:00:51.139 --> 00:00:55.404
Rule two: many owners take s, then the apostrophe.

00:00:55.404 --> 00:00:57.465
The campaign belongs to many residents.

00:00:58.543 --> 00:01:02.783
Rule three: words like children and women are already plural.

00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:05.733
So it's not childrens, apostrophe.

00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:07.938
It's children, apostrophe s.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.465
Let's try one.

00:01:10.465 --> 00:01:13.045
First, does the word own the next one?

00:01:13.045 --> 00:01:17.590
The campaign belongs to the residents, so yes, it's possessive.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.705
Next, is it one resident, or many?

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:23.140
A whole campaign suggests many.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.910
Choice A has no apostrophe at all.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.560
Choice B means just one resident.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.110
Choice D isn't standard English.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.835
For many owners, write s, then the apostrophe.

00:01:34.835 --> 00:01:35.886
The answer is C.

00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:39.603
Watch out for the plural apostrophe.

00:01:39.603 --> 00:01:42.783
If nothing is owned, there's no apostrophe.

00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:45.448
The dog's barked all night is wrong.

00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:46.397
Just the dogs.

00:01:47.448 --> 00:01:54.108
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the rules, and the trap.

00:01:54.108 --> 00:01:56.927
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
